0025:     3. For each chosen color, pick a source position satisfying trail-space bounds (blue needs c <= W-3 and r >= 1; red needs c >= 4; green needs r <= H-4; pink needs r >= 6).
0026:     4. Compute all trail cells, endpoints, and segments. Verify no cell collisions (trails/endpoints all land on distinct bg cells, except red-vertical crossing overlap on grey).
0027:     5. If red and a vertical marker both present, check for crossings; compute yellow diagonal from each crossing down-left to grid edge. Verify diagonal cells don't hit any source/endpoint.
0028:     6. If any collision, retry placement. Acceptance rate is high on 9-11 grids with 1-4 markers.
0029:     7. Input = black grid with only the source pixels placed. Output = input + grey trails + colored endpoints + yellow diagonals.

